147887323943662,"_gp_int_coverage":true,"_score_int_coverage":27.1,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":0.0,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":88.9,"_gate_accruals":-0.021567654034971594,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":29.8,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.0658176493843223,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":95.5,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.008417246590166669,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":89.5,"_gate_piotroski":6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":0.030705123168535797,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":15.4,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.4941003905616523,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":17.6,"_gate_incr_roic":0.1434693177922523,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":64.5,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.01185202708911949,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":29.4,"_gate_pool_share":0.17691115723805018,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.00980677002356467,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":29.9,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.15549437172334568,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":-0.009810445574054189,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":40.2,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.059278878339020014,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":77.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0517635363649116,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0054733427934319885,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":90.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.0074400003,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":5.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Textron Inc. operates in the aircraft, defense, industrial, and finance businesses worldwide. It operates in six segments: Textron Aviation, Bell, Textron Systems, Industrial, Textron eAviation, and Finance. The Textron Aviation segment manufactures, sells, and services business jets, turboprop and piston engine aircraft, and military trainer and defense aircraft, as well as offers maintenance, inspection, and repair services; commercial parts; and advanced flight training devices. The Bell segment supplies military and commercial helicopters, tiltrotor aircraft, and related spare parts and services. The Textron Systems segment offers unmanned aircraft systems, electronic systems and solutions, advanced marine crafts, piston aircraft engines, live military air-to-air and air-to-ship training, weapons and related components, and armored and specialty vehicles. The Industrial segment offers blow-molded solutions, including conventional plastic fuel tanks and pressurized fuel tanks; plastic tanks for catalytic reduction systems and other fuel system components; lightweight and composite pentatonic battery systems for use in electric vehicles primarily to automobile original equipment manufacturers; and golf cars, off-road utility vehicles, powersports products, light transportation vehicles, aviation ground support equipment, professional turf-maintenance equipment, and turf-care vehicles to golf courses and resorts, government agencies and municipalities, consumers, outdoor enthusiasts, and commercial and industrial users. The Textron eAviation segment manufactures and sells light aircraft and gliders with electric and combustion engines; and provides other research and development initiatives related to sustainable aviation solutions. The Finance segment offers financing services to purchase new and pre-owned aviation aircraft and Bell helicopters. Textron Inc. was founded in 1923 and is headquartered in Providence, Rhode Island.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Lisa M. Atherton | CEO, President & Director | Age 50","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 34K people. Revenue per employee of $435K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers. Each employee generates $27K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Textron Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $14.2B market cap on $14.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 9% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $929M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.42\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 6.1\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $22.6M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-22596999.88},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 28% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 25% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","42 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why Textron (TXT) is a Top Momentum Stock for the Long-Term","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029516/why-textron-txt-is-a-top-momentum-stock-for-the-long-term?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Czacks_education_momentum_score-3029516","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794577804.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Should Raised Earnings Guidance Require Action From Textron (TXT) Investors?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nyse-txt/textron/news/should-raised-earnings-guidance-require-action-from-textron-1","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575834.691,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Textron (TXT), What Is Behind The Fresh Attention Around It?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"ht